  "record": "T5 compositor, round 1\nT5-Q1: 1 (A small portable set: opaque, transparent, window_material, transient_material)\nT5-Q3: 1 (Both: the application allows a window to be non-opaque, and the theme chooses the backdrop)\nT5-Q5: 1 (A declared fallback chain ending at opaque, drawn by GUI.Forms)\nT5-Q6: 1 (The whole window receives input; no click-through in T5)\nT5-Q7: 1 (T5 builds a general preference signal: high contrast and reduced transparency)\nT5-Q16: 1 (Glass flattened to its tint over the background colour; reflections omitted)\nT5-Q14: 1 (The part's own engine raster only: face, material, glow; not its text)\nT5-Q15: 1 (8 logical units, the same cap as blur and glow)\nT5-Q2: 1 (Documented interfaces only)\nT5-Q4: 1 (Declared when the window is created; only the theme's grant changes at run time)\nT5-Q8: 1 (Through T3's @media, per window)\nT5-Q9: 1 (Link libXfixes and libXrender) — note: wayland is growing in popularity. we shipped on x11 because as we understood x11 programs work on wayland. linux is fragmented here, and i am not entirely confident how to proceed.\nT5-Q10: 1 (None in T5: X11 offers transparent only)\nT5-Q11: 1 (Not in T5)\nT5-Q12: 1 (Install xcompmgr in the Linux CI job; the gate test starts and stops it under Xvfb)\nT5-Q13: 1 (A renderer service every renderer implements, reported in its capabilities)"
